# Frontend Conventions

- Next.js App Router only, TypeScript strict mode. Server Components
  by default; add "use client" only when genuinely needed.
- State split: **TanStack Query** for anything from the backend
  (fetching, caching, mutations) — never fetch server data with
  useEffect+useState. **Zustand** only for pure UI state (selected
  branch, modal open/closed, sidebar collapsed). Never mix the two.
- All backend calls go through the shared API client in
  /frontend/lib/api.ts, which always sets `credentials: "include"` —
  never call fetch() directly against NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL elsewhere.
- shadcn/ui as the component base. Check /frontend/components/ui/
  before writing a new primitive from scratch.
- No new npm dependencies without asking first — the stack is
  intentionally minimal (Next.js, Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Zustand,
  TanStack Query, lucide-react).
- The public worker-facing pages (/app/s/[linkToken]/*) must never
  import the manager Sidebar layout or assume an authenticated
  session — they are a separate, unauthenticated surface.
